  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Yellow sand around a desert crater gushes down like tidal waves and fills the pit. Fang Yuan cannot dodge in time and is buried. On the now mirror-flat desert, the sand statue of a horned dragon appears. The statue coils, the dragon’s head bites its tail, and the surrounding sand gathers into a great force that suppresses him under the sand.",
      "chapters": [
        675
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She says the move forms an incomparable pressure on the enemy from all directions. Once trapped, they cannot move until they are turned into meat paste. In the past she forcefully suppressed a desolate beast evil dragon with it. She values it at least three immortal essence stones in treasure yellow heaven. Using Hair Armor and his immortal zombie body, Fang Yuan takes the pressure without injury. The dragon statue cracks, disintegrates, and he bursts out of the sand.",
      "chapters": [
        675
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "move_hair_armor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan classifies mortal killer moves worth three immortal essence stones as middle tier, reliable methods. He names Plump Lady’s burial dragon sand coffin as valued at three immortal essence stones.",
